msgstr "Substituting `N = 1073741824` yields:"

msgid "因此，如果 `BLOCK_SIZE` 按2的幂取值，至少应设置为 `32768`。"
msgstr "Therefore, if `BLOCK_SIZE` takes values that are powers of 2, set it to at least `32768`."

msgid "优化前的代码："
msgstr "Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后的代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "动态计算适合的BLOCK_SIZE以避免coreDim超限"
msgstr "Dynamically calculate a suitable BLOCK_SIZE to avoid coreDim exceeding the limit"

msgid "处理复合问题：coreDim + UB溢出"
msgstr "Handling compound problems: coreDim + UB overflow"

msgid "问题分析： 在某些情况下，解决了coreDim问题后可能引发新的UB溢出问题。这通常发生在增大BLOCK_SIZE后，单个线程块需要处理的数据量超出了NPU的UB缓存容量。"
msgstr "Problem analysis: In some cases, resolving the coreDim issue may trigger a new UB overflow issue. This usually occurs after increasing BLOCK_SIZE, when the data a single thread block must process exceeds the UB cache capacity of the NPU."

msgid "案例： 数据规模：N = 1073741824，原始BLOCK_SIZE = 4096，计算得到的coreDim = 262144 > 65535（超限），调整为BLOCK_SIZE = 32768后，coreDim = 32768（合规），但出现UB溢出"
msgstr "Case: Data size: N = 1073741824, original BLOCK_SIZE = 4096, the calculated coreDim = 262144 > 65535 (exceeds the limit). After adjusting to BLOCK_SIZE = 32768, coreDim = 32768 (compliant), but UB overflow occurs."

msgid "解决思路： 引入BLOCK_SIZE_SUB参数，将大块进一步细分，在保持合理coreDim的同时控制内存使用。 优化前代码："
msgstr "Solution: Introduce the BLOCK_SIZE_SUB parameter to further subdivide large blocks, controlling memory usage while maintaining a reasonable coreDim. Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "为什么会出现UBSIZE超出内存的错误"
msgstr "Why does the UBSIZE exceed memory error occur?"

msgid "切分不合理，存在过多的非对齐访存或者运算，例如对(64, 32)二维数据搬运，对应stride(128, 32)，如果是对齐数据的访存，对应的stride(32, 1)。对于非对齐访问内容，在最内轴新增一个大小为1的轴，变为(64, 32, 4)，由于硬件要求vector算子场景ub内存32Byte对齐，假设type=float16，对应stride应该为(12832, 128, 1)"
msgstr "Improper tiling results in excessive non-aligned memory accesses or operations. For example, for (64, 32) 2D data movement, the corresponding stride is (128, 32). If the data access is aligned, the corresponding stride is (32, 1). For non-aligned data access, add an axis of size 1 to the innermost axis, changing the shape to (64, 32, 4). Because the hardware requires 32-byte alignment for UB memory in vector operator scenarios, assuming type=float16, the corresponding stride should be (12832, 128, 1)."

msgid "离散访存代码逐行对比观察scalar低效映射"
msgstr "Let's compare the discrete memory access code line by line to observe the inefficient scalar mapping."

msgid "设置环境变量TRITON_DEBUG=1，保存~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter，然后执行"
msgstr "Set the environment variable TRITON_DEBUG=1, save ~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter, and then execute"

msgid "会有输出IR，对比Triton算子逻辑与IR内部的操作，观察是否有未映射成指令的操作。 观察HIVM IR阶段是否存在纯scalar搬运或者计算，没有映射为SIMD指令，这会成为性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "The IR is output. Compare the Triton operator logic with the operations inside the IR, and check whether there are operations that are not mapped to instructions. Check whether there is pure scalar data movement or computation in the HIVM IR stage that is not mapped to SIMD instructions, as this becomes a performance bottleneck."

msgid "问题：离散访存 && scalar低效映射 b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]  Triton原先写法利用thread的方式对[1024,32]中的最低维度32绑定线程块，再对1024切16，分为[64，16，32]，再对64绑定线程块"
msgstr "Problem: Discrete memory access and inefficient scalar mapping b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]  The original Triton implementation uses a thread-based approach to bind thread blocks to the lowest dimension 32 in [1024, 32]. It then splits 1024 by 16 into [64, 16, 32], and binds thread blocks to 64."

msgid "优化思路"
msgstr "Optimization approach"

msgid "调整block_ptr的shape/stride: 把 (1024, 32) 看成二维矩阵，最低维度32是连续的，所以stride应该是 (32, 1)，而不是 (32,)，这样每个线程块能访问连续的32元素。让线程块绑定到行维度（1024），每个线程处理一整行的32元素。这样访存就是连续的，亲和性好。"
msgstr "Adjust the shape/stride of block_ptr: Treat (1024, 32) as a two-dimensional matrix. The lowest dimension 32 is contiguous, so the stride should be (32, 1) instead of (32,). This way, each thread block can access 32 contiguous elements. Bind the thread block to the row dimension (1024), and each thread processes an entire row of 32 elements. This ensures contiguous memory access and good affinity."

